<title>SPAIN: Spain labour minister sees 300,000 new jobs in '98.</title>
<headline>Spain labour minister sees 300,000 new jobs in '98.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Labour Minister Javier Arenas said on Thursday that data for July will show it was a very positive month for employment.</p>
<p>Arenas told journalists he foresees jobs growth of 2.5 percent or 300,000 new jobs next year.</p>
<p>&quot;The evolution of July numbers shows that it was a very positive month for employment,&quot; Arenas said.  </p>
<p>Arenas predicted jobs growth of about 300,000 in 1998 and a similar rate of growth in the following years.</p>
<p>&quot;With respect to 1998, the forecast is for 2.5 percent (jobs growth). I believe that in the coming years, it could grow by more than 300,000 jobs a year,&quot; Arenas said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
